Helpdesk one pager: second sign in step rollout

What changed
- Everyone must register a second sign in step (Microsoft Authenticator) by
  {{ registration_deadline }}.
- From {{ enforcement_day }}, sign in requires the second step. Until then,
  policies run in report-only mode and block nobody.

Common calls and what to do

1. "I keep getting a registration prompt."
   That is expected. Walk the caller through registering the Microsoft
   Authenticator app; it takes about two minutes and the prompts stop.

2. "I cannot sign in at all."
   Check whether the caller has registered a second step. If they have not,
   {% if uses_tap %}create a Temporary Access Pass for them (Users, then
   Authentication methods, then Add authentication method), read it to them
   by voice, and stay on the line while they register.{% else %}escalate to
   the rollout owner before changing anything.{% endif %}

3. "My old email app stopped working."
   Older apps that cannot do the second step are being retired. Move the
   caller to Outlook or the web mailbox. If the app belongs to a system, not
   a person, escalate to the rollout owner; do not create exceptions
   yourself.

4. "I lost my phone."
   {% if uses_tap %}Verify the caller's identity by an agreed second channel,
   then issue a Temporary Access Pass so they can register a new device.
   {% else %}Verify the caller's identity by an agreed second channel, then
   escalate to the rollout owner to reset their sign in methods.{% endif %}

Escalation
- Anything involving an account that runs software (a service account), an
  executive, or a shared mailbox goes to the rollout owner before any change.
- Never remove an account from a security policy to fix a call. That is a
  rollout owner decision and it is logged.
